# Tool Input Validation

| Field  | Value                |
| ------ | -------------------- |
| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | In Progress          |

Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.

## Validation at execute time

- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required, includes its full path when nested, escapes JSON Pointer separators in property names, and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16), [validated by: names the full path of a missing nested property (specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#3)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L56), [validated by: escapes separators in missing property paths (specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#3)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L83), [validated by: returns a required-field rejection before executing (specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#3)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L104)).
- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults. When `input` violates an `enum` constraint, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a rejection and logs the failing field path and constraint without including the supplied value or invoking the executor ([validated by: rejects an enum mismatch before executing (specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#5)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L16)).
- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.
- When a tool explicitly forbids additional properties in its schema, a rejection names the unexpected property's path and the additional-properties constraint without exposing its value ([validated by: names a forbidden extra property without exposing its value (specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#7)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L119)).

## Schema compilation and caching

- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: reuses the static schema compiled at registration (specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#9)](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L71)).
- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules.

## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery

- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
import {createChatOrchestrator} from './chatOrchestrator.js';
import type {OrchestratorHooks} from './chatOrchestrator.js';
import type {AIProvider, MessageChunk, SendMessageParams, UsageMetadata} from '../types/ai.js';
import {AIError} from '../types/ai.js';
import type {ChatSession} from '../types/session.js';
import {PromptBuilder} from '../infrastructure/builders/promptBuilder.js';
import {ToolRegistry} from './tools/registry.js';
import type {ToolResponse} from './tools/registry.js';
import type {OutgoingMessage} from '../types/messages.js';
import type {SessionEntry} from '../types/session.js';

// Fixed: nothing asserts on it, and new Date() would tie the run to the clock.
const SENT_AT = '2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z';

// One expect per test needs the rejection as a value rather than a matcher.
const outcomeOf = (call: Promise<unknown>): Promise<string> =>
  call.then(() => 'resolved without throwing').catch((error: Error) => error.message);

function createSession(content: string): ChatSession {
  return {
    sessionId: 's1',
    userId: 'u1',
    entries: [{role: 'user', content, timestamp: SENT_AT}],
  };
}

function createMockProvider(response: string, usage?: UsageMetadata): AIProvider {
  return {
    async *sendMessage(_params: SendMessageParams): AsyncGenerator<MessageChunk> {
      yield {type: 'text', text: response};
      yield {type: 'stop', stopReason: 'end_turn', usage};
    },
    async generateStructured<T>(): Promise<T> {
      return {} as T;
    },
  };
}

function createErrorProvider(error: Error): AIProvider {
  return {
    // eslint-disable-next-line require-yield
    async *sendMessage(): AsyncGenerator<MessageChunk> {
      throw error;
    },
    async generateStructured<T>(): Promise<T> {
      return {} as T;
    },
  };
}

const promptBuilder = new PromptBuilder({identity: 'You are a test assistant.'});

type RecordedHook =
  | 'beforeSession'
  | 'beforeUserInput'
  | 'afterUserInput'
  | 'beforeModelResponse'
  | 'afterModelResponse'
  | 'afterSession'
  | 'onError';

// Only the named hooks are installed: one that merely exists changes the observed order.
const recordingHooks = (callOrder: string[], names: RecordedHook[]): OrchestratorHooks => {
  const all: Required<OrchestratorHooks> = {
    beforeSession: async () => void callOrder.push('beforeSession'),
    beforeUserInput: async (_session, msg) => {
      callOrder.push('beforeUserInput');
      return msg;
    },
    afterUserInput: async () => void callOrder.push('afterUserInput'),
    beforeModelResponse: async (_session, systemPrompt) => {
      callOrder.push('beforeModelResponse');
      return systemPrompt;
    },
    afterModelResponse: async () => void callOrder.push('afterModelResponse'),
    afterSession: async () => void callOrder.push('afterSession'),
    onError: async () => void callOrder.push('onError'),
  };

  return Object.fromEntries(names.map(name => [name, all[name]])) as OrchestratorHooks;
};

// Records what the orchestrator actually sent, for tests that assert on the request.
const capturingProvider = (): {provider: AIProvider; sent: {systemPrompt: string; lastUserContent: string}} => {
  const sent = {systemPrompt: '', lastUserContent: ''};

  return {
    sent,
    provider: {
      async *sendMessage(params: SendMessageParams): AsyncGenerator<MessageChunk> {
        sent.systemPrompt = params.systemPrompt;
        const last = params.messages[params.messages.length - 1];
        sent.lastUserContent = typeof last.content === 'string' ? last.content : '';
        yield {type: 'text', text: 'ok'};
        yield {type: 'stop', stopReason: 'end_turn'};
      },
      async generateStructured<T>(): Promise<T> {
        return {} as T;
      },
    },
  };
};

describe('ChatOrchestrator hooks', () => {
  describe('beforeSession', () => {
    it('called before anything else', async () => {
      const callOrder: string[] = [];
      const hooks = recordingHooks(callOrder, ['beforeSession', 'beforeUserInput', 'beforeModelResponse']);

      const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(createMockProvider('hi'), promptBuilder, undefined, {hooks});
      await orchestrator.processMessage(createSession('hello'));

      expect(callOrder[0]).toBe('beforeSession');
    });
  });

  describe('afterSession', () => {
    it('called after everything completes', async () => {
      const callOrder: string[] = [];
      const hooks = recordingHooks(callOrder, ['afterModelResponse', 'afterSession']);

      const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(createMockProvider('hi'), promptBuilder, undefined, {hooks});
      await orchestrator.processMessage(createSession('hello'));

      expect(callOrder).toEqual(['afterModelResponse', 'afterSession']);
    });

    it('called even when an error occurs', async () => {
      let afterSessionCalled = false;
      const hooks: OrchestratorHooks = {
        onError: async () => {},
        afterSession: async () => {
          afterSessionCalled = true;
        },
      };

      const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(createErrorProvider(new Error('boom')), promptBuilder, undefined, {
        hooks,
      });
      const outcome = await outcomeOf(orchestrator.processMessage(createSession('hello')));

      expect({outcome, afterSessionCalled}).toEqual({outcome: 'boom', afterSessionCalled: true});
    });
  });

  describe('beforeUserInput', () => {
    it('receives the last user message content', async () => {
      let receivedMessage = '';
      const hooks: OrchestratorHooks = {
        beforeUserInput: async (_session, userMessage) => {
          receivedMessage = userMessage;
          return userMessage;
        },
      };

      const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(createMockProvider('ok'), promptBuilder, undefined, {hooks});
      await orchestrator.processMessage(createSession('my answer'));

      expect(receivedMessage).toBe('my answer');
    });

    it('modifies user message when returning different value', async () => {
      const {provider, sent} = capturingProvider();

      const hooks: OrchestratorHooks = {
        beforeUserInput: async (_session, _msg) => 'sanitized input',
      };

      const orchestrator = createChatOrchestrator(provider, promptBuilder, undefined, {hooks});
      await orchestrator.processMessage(createSession('raw input'));

      expect(sent.lastUserContent).toBe('sanitized input');
